  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "As of **September 2026**, the collection and soft brands most commonly evaluated for hotel conversions in the Caribbean and Latin America include:\n\n| Hotel group | Commonly considered brands | Typical positioning |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Marriott International** | **Autograph Collection**, **Tribute Portfolio**, **The Luxury Collection** | Upper-upscale through luxury; particularly relevant for distinctive resorts and all-inclusive conversions. Marriott is actively using all three in the Caribbean. ([marriott.com](https://www.marriott.com/marriott-brands/portfolio/cala-openings?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Hilton** | **Curio Collection by Hilton**, **Tapestry Collection by Hilton**, **LXR Hotels & Resorts** | Tapestry for upscale; Curio for upper-upscale/lifestyle; LXR for independent luxury. Curio and Tapestry have substantial conversion activity across CALA. ([stories.hilton.com](https://stories.hilton.com/releases/hilton-wraps-2024-with-record-portfolio-and-pipeline-growth-in-the-caribbean-and-latin-america?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Hyatt** | **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt**, **JdV by Hyatt**; increasingly **Unscripted by Hyatt** | Unbound for upper-upscale/luxury landmark properties; JdV for lifestyle hotels; Unscripted is a newer, conversion-friendly upscale option. ([hyatt.com](https://www.hyatt.com/development/ourbrands/theunboundcollectionbyhyatt?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **IHG Hotels & Resorts** | **Vignette Collection**, **voco hotels** | Vignette is the principal luxury/lifestyle soft brand; voco is a more standardized but highly conversion-oriented premium option. ([ihgplc.com](https://www.ihgplc.com/en/news-and-media/news-releases/2025/ihg-hotels-and-resorts-conversion-friendly-brands-fuel-growth-opportunities-for-owners?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Accor** | **MGallery**, **Emblems Collection**, **Handwritten Collection** | Handwritten at upscale, MGallery at upper-upscale boutique and Emblems at luxury; designed to retain each hotel’s identity. ([group.accor.com](https://group.accor.com/en/hotel-development?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Wyndham Hotels & Resorts** | **Registry Collection Hotels**, **Trademark Collection by Wyndham**, occasionally **Dolce Hotels & Resorts** | Registry for luxury resorts; Trademark for upper-midscale/upscale independents; Dolce for resort, spa and meetings-oriented properties. ([development.wyndhamhotels.com](https://development.wyndhamhotels.com/convert-your-existing-hotel?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Choice Hotels** | **Ascend Hotel Collection**, **Radisson Individuals** | Ascend for upscale boutique, historic and resort conversions; Radisson Individuals for upper-upscale full-service hotels. ([choicehotelsdevelopment.com](https://www.choicehotelsdevelopment.com/sfsites/c/cms/delivery/media/MCUMJCKAM4XNGDBGYQ36NVQN55WE?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **BWH Hotels** | **BW Premier Collection**, **BW Signature Collection**, **WorldHotels Collections** | Flexible alternatives from mid-upscale through luxury, sometimes considered where major-chain economics or territorial restrictions are problematic. ([development.bwhhotels.com](https://development.bwhhotels.com/signature?utm_source=openai)) |\n\n### Typical first-call shortlist\n\nFor a conventional **upper-upscale Caribbean or Latin American conversion**, the most frequent competitive set is:\n\n1. **Autograph Collection**\n2. **Curio Collection**\n3. **Tribute Portfolio**\n4. **The Unbound Collection**\n5. **Vignette Collection**\n6. **MGallery**\n\nFor a **luxury resort**, owners generally add:\n\n- **The Luxury Collection**\n- **LXR Hotels & Resorts**\n- **Registry Collection**\n- **Emblems Collection**\n- **WorldHotels Luxury**\n- Independent affiliations such as **Leading Hotels of the World** or **Small Luxury Hotels of the World**. ([development.bwhhotels.com](https://development.bwhhotels.com/content/luxury-hotels/en_US/hotel-development/development-collections.html?utm_source=openai))\n\nThe practical shortlist ultimately depends on the hotel’s **ADR target, room count, renovation budget, all-inclusive status, destination, existing brand-area restrictions, management-versus-franchise structure, and the strength of each loyalty platform’s regional demand**. Emerging brands such as Hilton’s **Outset Collection** and Hyatt’s **Unscripted** may also enter discussions, but they currently have less operating history in CALA than the established collections above. ([stories.hilton.com](https://stories.hilton.com/releases/launch-of-outset-collection-by-hilton?utm_source=openai))",
